# ouroboros#143 (closure pin): a top-level `for` variable that shadows an
# existing module global is LOOP-SCOPED in the VM -- the body reads the
# binder, the global is untouched afterwards. The AOT once reused the global
# (acc accumulated 5+5+5 = 15, VM 3). The first line matched then too, so a
# fixture checking only the post-loop value would have passed: the body read
# is the discriminating line. Both the read-only body and a body that writes
# the binder, plus a nested loop reusing the same name.
i is 5
acc is 0
for i in range of 3:
    acc is acc + i
print of i
print of acc
j is 100
for j in range of 3:
    j is j + 10
    acc is acc + j
print of j
print of acc
for i in range of 2:
    for i in range of 3:
        acc is acc + i
print of i
print of acc
